2. Create a constant system logging profile that maps an IP address alongside a server port
number inside a tuple pair, demonstrating that these settings remain secure from runtime
modification attempts.



# Store IP address and port number in a tuple
logging_profile = ("192.168.1.10", 8080)

# Unpack the tuple
ip_address, port = logging_profile

print("IP Address:", ip_address)
print("Server Port:", port)

# Try to modify the tuple
try:
    logging_profile[0] = "192.168.1.20"
except TypeError:
    print("Error: Tuple cannot be modified!")
